File Index

/consider.ts
Purpose: The seven sentences of do_consider (act_info.c) read exactly, with the level difference each stands for; a line that is not one of them is not an answer, nothing is guessed. MAX_FIGHT_LEVEL_DIFF (4) is the rule of the leveling fights: a fight starts only up to "do you feel lucky".

/condition.ts
Purpose: The eight sentences of the battle prompt and look (comm.c, act_info.c) as ranges of percent of hit points; the game never shows the number, so every reading is a range. 100 means exactly full health, 99 is already "a few scratches".

/damage.ts
Purpose: dam_message (fight.c) as damage ranges per verb, for the four message shapes the character takes part in (its own plain blow, its skill or spell, a plain blow at it, a skill at it) and immunity. Blows between two other creatures never match. "You hit yourself" is not a fight.

/monitor.ts
Purpose: Follows a fight from the feed with no model and says where it is going: damage per round, the opponent's estimated hit points (from what was dealt against how hurt it looks), rounds to kill and to die, advice, and a projection to the time of the question because the model is always behind (a round is 3 s, merc.h PULSE_VIOLENCE). The character's own hit points are exact; everything about the opponent is an estimate and reliable says so. A fight with 4 rounds of silence is over, and snapshot() closes it. finish advice needs reliable data, one round of text is not enough.

/knowledge.ts
Purpose: What Copilot knows about monsters (archive lookup, consider answer), per room and per keyword, bounded and expiring. Two keywords are the same target when one is a prefix of the other, because the game matches a typed word as a prefix of a name.

/gate.ts
Purpose: The rule that keeps Copilot out of a blind fight, as a pure decision for one command: allow, look up (archive), consider, or deny. A short form is read as an attack when it could start one (the game reads it by its own table order, which this package does not have) unless it is exactly another command; an empty word is a prefix of every name and must never be resolved (a test found that). rescue and assist name an ally, not a monster.

/considerTracker.ts
Purpose: Records the game's answer to a consider typed by anyone, for the room and keyword it was typed in; the answer must come right after the command (10 s), and another command, a move or a close forgets it. con is typed as consider, every prefix of at least three letters.

/offensiveSpells.ts
Purpose: GENERATED by scripts/gen-offensive-spells.mjs from merc-area's stock skill table (target 1 is TAR_CHAR_OFFENSIVE); a node test fails when the list is stale.
